{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mrk-10-1","title":"Mark 10:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ disputes with the Pharisees touching divorcement: 13 blesses the children that are brought unto him; 17 resolves a rich man how he may inherit life everlasting; 23 tells his disciples of the danger of riches; 28 promises rewards to them that forsake any thing for the gospel; 32 foretells his death and resurrection; 35 bids the two ambitious suitors to think rather of suffering with him; 46 and restores to Bartimaeus his sight.</p>\n<p>A.M. 4033. A.D. 29. he arose. Mt 19:1-12 by. Joh 10:40; 11:7 he taught. Ec 12:9; Jer 32:33; Joh 18:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-10-2","title":"Mark 10:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>the Pharisees. 8:15; Mt 9:34; 15:12; 23:13; Lu 5:30; 6:7; 7:30; 11:39,53,54; 16:14 Joh 7:32,48; 11:47,57 Is it. Mal 2:16; Mt 5:31,32; 19:3; 1Co 7:10,11 tempting. 8:11; Mt 16:1; 22:35; Joh 8:6; 1Co 10:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-10-3","title":"Mark 10:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>What. Isa 8:20; Lu 10:25; Joh 5:39; Ga 4:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-10-4","title":"Mark 10:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>De 24:1-4; Isa 50:1; Jer 3:1; Mt 1:19; 5:31,32; 19:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-10-5","title":"Mark 10:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>For. De 9:6; 31:27; Ne 9:16,17,26; Mt 19:8; Ac 7:51; Heb 3:7-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mrk-10-6","title":"Mark 10:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MRK","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":